# EVE-OS USB CDC-ECM gadget auto-bring-up rule for NVIDIA Spark (HP ZGX Nano G1n).
#
# When piKVM is connected via USB OTG to the Spark device, the kernel creates a
# usb0 (cdc_ether) interface. This rule ensures the interface is brought UP
# automatically so EVE's nim can use it as a management path for initial
# controller connectivity before physical ethernet is configured.
#
# The piKVM dnsmasq assigns 172.30.30.x via DHCP and advertises DNS servers
# (8.8.8.8, 8.8.4.4) so EVE can resolve zedcloud.alpha.zededa.net.
#
# Prerequisite on piKVM: /usr/lib/python3.13/site-packages/kvmd/apps/__init__.py
# must have "--dhcp-option=6,8.8.8.8,8.8.4.4" (not just "--dhcp-option=6").
# See: pkg/pillar/docs/zededa-spark-pikvm-setup.md

SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", KERNEL=="usb0", \
  DRIVERS=="cdc_ether", \
  RUN+="/sbin/ip link set usb0 up"
